<ProjectLayout slug="vis-a-vis-verification">
  <p>
    The process of “vis-a-vis verification” is fundamentally concerned with 
    the way in which relationships of trust are established within a system. 
    For this, it is necessary that a real social interaction takes place 
    between an already verified person and a person newly added to the system;
     that is, both individuals stand “vis-a-vis,” face to face with one another, 
     and perform a specific action.
  </p>

  <p>
    Not all individuals can be incorporated into the feedback loop. Some are
     too fragile and risk breaking, while others are too strong and could cause something to break.
  </p>

<p>
    These forms of becoming presuppose that, in a moment of experience, bodies pass through the 
    feeling that it could suddenly all be over—at the ends of the world or of human beings.
  </p>

